  "rationale": "Chick Corea's debut as a leader is a blazing advanced hard-bop set that announced one of the defining pianists of the post-bop era. The Penguin Guide to Jazz awards it 4 stars, AllMusic 4.5 stars, and DownBeat's Harvey Pekar gave it 4.5 stars calling it 'a splendid record.' The quintet of Corea, Woody Shaw, Joe Farrell, Steve Swallow, and Joe Chambers represents a generational crossroads \u2014 Corea's sidemen from the Willie Bobo and Mongo Santamaria bands stepping out together. The title track became a jazz classic and 'Litha' was later recorded by Stan Getz. Strong consensus: Penguin Guide core collection, AllMusic indispensable, DownBeat 4.5 stars. Inside the 1940-1979 scope window, clearly post-bop/hard-bop with no fusion elements yet audible.",
